written for chimimouryou (https://github.com/blankiekun/chimimouryou) and moved
here; none of it is ported from ッツ Ebook Reader or from Jiten.

yurigana/kanji-readings.json (on and kun readings of 常用 and 人名用 kanji) is
derived from KANJIDIC2 by the Electronic Dictionary Research and Development
Group (https://www.edrdg.org/kanjidic/), licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/); it is distributed under the
same licence. tools/kanji_readings.py builds it.

yurigana/jmdict-pairs.json.gz (written forms and their readings) is derived from
JMdict by the Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group
(https://www.edrdg.org/jmdict/j_jmdict.html), licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/); it is distributed under the
same licence. tools/jmdict_pairs.py builds it; the file records the JMdict
version (its creation date) it was built from.

yurigana/reading-model-public.json.gz is a model trained on public-domain works
from Aozora Bunko (https://www.aozora.gr.jp/) and on sentences with reviewed
readings from Tatoeba (https://tatoeba.org/), by Tatoeba's contributors,
licensed under CC BY 2.0 FR; neither text is included.

yurigana/default-readings.tsv (form, Sudachi's reading, reading given instead,
with counts) is derived from NDL Lab's huriganacorpus-aozora
(https://github.com/ndl-lab/huriganacorpus-aozora, readings of Aozora Bunko's
public-domain works; no known copyright restrictions), Tatoeba's transcriptions
(CC BY 2.0 FR) and JMdict by the Electronic
Dictionary Research and Development Group (https://www.edrdg.org/jmdict/),
licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/);
it is distributed under the same licence. tools/default_readings.py builds it;
no text is included.

yurigana/tatoeba-b2-ids.txt.gz lists the IDs of Tatoeba sentences that
yurigana.evaluate reports on; no sentence text is included.

eval/sanity.tsv, the regression list, holds sentences from Tatoeba (CC BY 2.0
FR; the note column gives each one's sentence id) and readings taken from JMdict
by the Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group
(https://www.edrdg.org/jmdict/j_jmdict.html, CC BY-SA 4.0); the file is
distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0.

The reading list the tools and Reader(known=...) take is not included. The
numbers in README.md were measured with Jiten's frequency list
(https://jiten.moe/frequency-dictionaries), which is not distributed here.

yurigana depends on SudachiPy (Apache License 2.0) and SudachiDict-full
(Apache License 2.0, Works Applications), installed separately by pip.
